{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/767605-dragon-wars-and-crossover","id":767605,"title":"Dragon Wars and Crossover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-16T23:37:22-08:00","id":767605,"title":"Dragon Wars and Crossover","content":"So with the new chapter added in Shattered Dreams we have a brief overview of the Dragon Empires, their technology and their colapse. I feel like there's some sort of crossover between between the realm of Mnemesis and the Dreaming or Awakened Magic but I am not quite sure how to parse it out.. any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T03:26:23-08:00","id":767713,"title":"","content":"Watching this thread with interest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T10:39:09-08:00","id":767936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/767605-dragon-wars-and-crossover#post767605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with the new chapter added in Shattered Dreams we have a brief overview of the Dragon Empires, their technology and their colapse. I feel like there's some sort of crossover between between the realm of Mnemesis and the Dreaming or Awakened Magic but I am not quite sure how to parse it out.. any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>what exactly are you trying to parse out? if we are to assume that the Dreaming and the Mnesis are the same thing, then the Dreaming is not closed off as Changelings believe. SD refers to it as spiritual scar tissue, the realm was destroyed when the Gauntlet formed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T11:34:03-08:00","id":767970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/767605-dragon-wars-and-crossover?p=767936#post767936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> what exactly are you trying to parse out? if we are to assume that the Dreaming and the Mnesis are the same thing, then the Dreaming is not closed off as Changelings believe. SD refers to it as spiritual scar tissue, the realm was destroyed when the Gauntlet formed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I was thinking Maybe the Dreaming is some sort of &quot;replacement&quot; for the Realm of Mnesis they seem to be conceptually very similar, or possibly many aspects of the High Umbra according to Mage. On the other hand while there aren't specific ties the Dragon King Empire looks a lot like how Awakened magick pushes stuff forward in theory at least. Plus I almost feel like &quot;Ancient Dinosaur Kingdoms&quot; is something that would be able to get more conceptual play out in Mage than anything outside time travel plot in werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T12:33:16-08:00","id":768015,"title":"","content":"Maybe it was a remnant of Mnesis. It was the last little bit of what used to be and the rise of human dreams filled it with the first Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:47:32-08:00","id":769236,"title":"","content":"Mnesis as it appears in the Dragon King chapter seems to be an after effect of Gaia's dreams that the Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm made reality. The ability of the Dragon Kings to harness that energy was Gaia's ultimate gift to her first born changers. The Dragon Kings instead of cherishing and nurturing Mnesis instead abused it and there fellow ancient shifters. Now the Mokole are left with a pale substitute memories most of which are fractured perhaps even more than has been presented. The Mokole remember the Wonder Work that ended the age of the Dragon Kings never realizing that the Wonder Work was a bloody useless Civil War. I would hesitate to use Mnesis as the source of the Dreaming. I might use it as the foundation of the Abyss however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T18:53:28-08:00","id":769710,"title":"","content":"Before this book I kicked around the idea of having the Kings responsible for the Weaver going insane. I was going to run a time travel arc where the group got to meet the Kings at the height of their power and development. Not wanting the good times to end, many of the more spiritually gifted Kings were going to create a rite and use it in hopes of manipulating the Weaver to freeze their society at this stage, hoping to avoid a downfall. The would cause the Weaver to glitch out, trap the Wyrm, drive it insane and BOOM Wonder Work and the eventual Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T20:54:20-08:00","id":769745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/767605-dragon-wars-and-crossover?p=769236#post769236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mnesis as it appears in the Dragon King chapter seems to be an after effect of Gaia's dreams that the Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm made reality. The ability of the Dragon Kings to harness that energy was Gaia's ultimate gift to her first born changers. The Dragon Kings instead of cherishing and nurturing Mnesis instead abused it and there fellow ancient shifters. Now the Mokole are left with a pale substitute memories most of which are fractured perhaps even more than has been presented. The Mokole remember the Wonder Work that ended the age of the Dragon Kings never realizing that the Wonder Work was a bloody useless Civil War. I would hesitate to use Mnesis as the source of the Dreaming. I might use it as the foundation of the Abyss however.</div> </div> </div> </div>'<br /> <br /> I don't think its a 1 for 1 thing but I feel like there's some serious conceptual overlap between what the Dragon Kings did and Mage Magick. All Dragon King &quot;technology&quot; past paelolithic required Mnemsis, the same MIGHT be true for humanity and Magick. And the whole Realm of Ideas and Dreams sounds like the Dreaming or High umbra. I know its not meant to have an explicit connection it just feels like there's some concepts that seem very similar so some connection might be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T21:21:01-08:00","id":769756,"title":"","content":"By making Mnesis survive as the high umbra, and the Dreaming I think you are missing a central point. The Dragon Kings screwed up. They broke the way the world was supposed to work. The Mokole of today have exactly two connections to the former power that was the Dragon Kings: One a Mokole dreams his Archid form, this is the last vestige of Mnesis in &quot;modern times&quot;. The second is far more insidious and dangerous, The Innocents remember the twisted children, yes they exist and they are more than pissed, why they are Momma's little helpers punishing again and again the Mokole for actions they no longer remember. The Abyss as the corpse of Mnesis is far more thematic and at least in my opinion fits far better than trying to shoehorn Mages and Changeling into Werewolf's cosmology and history. I understand your views I disagree with you. Parallel evolution exists, and that appears to be the case here or the Weaver stole the idea when she was busy teaching the apes how to manipulate reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T01:37:46-08:00","id":769814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/767605-dragon-wars-and-crossover?p=769756#post769756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By making Mnesis survive as the high umbra, and the Dreaming I think you are missing a central point. The Dragon Kings screwed up. They broke the way the world was supposed to work. The Mokole of today have exactly two connections to the former power that was the Dragon Kings: One a Mokole dreams his Archid form, this is the last vestige of Mnesis in &quot;modern times&quot;. The second is far more insidious and dangerous, The Innocents remember the twisted children, yes they exist and they are more than pissed, why they are Momma's little helpers punishing again and again the Mokole for actions they no longer remember. The Abyss as the corpse of Mnesis is far more thematic and at least in my opinion fits far better than trying to shoehorn Mages and Changeling into Werewolf's cosmology and history. I understand your views I disagree with you. Parallel evolution exists, and that appears to be the case here or the Weaver stole the idea when she was busy teaching the apes how to manipulate reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think we are talking past eachother. I am familiar with the thematics of the chapter. It works well when the Mokole/Fera are center stage. But I made a separate thread to get people's ideas in a more crossover type setting. Are the Formorians the Shattered bits of Nightmare formed from the broken remains of the Dragon wars? is Humanity born with a spark of Stolen Mnemesis? Is that what an Avatar is? I get entirely what its trying to do its why I'm not weighing down the standard thread with it but rather seeing other uses for the idea of the Dragon Wars how they might come into play for other options.<br /> <br /> I Just thought since more people here might have read it more ideas might come from here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T08:19:24-08:00","id":770010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/767605-dragon-wars-and-crossover?p=769814#post769814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think we are talking past eachother. I am familiar with the thematics of the chapter. It works well when the Mokole/Fera are center stage. But I made a separate thread to get people's ideas in a more crossover type setting. Are the Formorians the Shattered bits of Nightmare formed from the broken remains of the Dragon wars? is Humanity born with a spark of Stolen Mnemesis? Is that what an Avatar is? I get entirely what its trying to do its why I'm not weighing down the standard thread with it but rather seeing other uses for the idea of the Dragon Wars how they might come into play for other options.<br /> <br /> I Just thought since more people here might have read it more ideas might come from here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf put a foot down about crossover with Changeling in Rokea. Qyrl found something in an unknown portion of the cosmos, Nightmare, and wished it into a form reminiscent of Chtulhu before being forced by Sea to shrink it down (which was when the Murdhuacha were spawned).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T18:34:33-08:00","id":773562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/767605-dragon-wars-and-crossover?p=769745#post769745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think its a 1 for 1 thing but I feel like there's some serious conceptual overlap between what the Dragon Kings did and Mage Magick. All Dragon King &quot;technology&quot; past paelolithic required Mnemsis, the same MIGHT be true for humanity and Magick. And the whole Realm of Ideas and Dreams sounds like the Dreaming or High umbra. I know its not meant to have an explicit connection it just feels like there's some concepts that seem very similar so some connection might be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one am picking up what you're putting down. There are definitely some parallels in there to MtAsc (and a little to MtAw, too!) - glorious towers (or dragon spires, if you like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), hubris, imagination turning into reality, magical god kings, etc. etc. etc.<br /> <br /> None of it is explicit, quite intentionally. At the very least, though, I can tell you I was reading a LOT of Mage20 while I was writing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":2653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","user":"NateD","date":". 11-24-2015, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}